              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ldegrez"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great recipe. I have made it twice, and both times increased the amount of horseradish. HOWEVER, the amount needed depends greatly on the quality of the horseradish used. The first time i made it I tripled the amount, the second time I used a higher quality product and only added 1/2 tbs more. I let it set for three hours. Delicious",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-18T05:35:38.260Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "debby loch"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I wanted to try a recipe without mayonnaise.. So I basically used my own fresh horseradish soaking in vinegar. I spooned out about 5 big tablespoons,and added approx 3/4 cup of sour cream,and added a few tablespoons of lemon... I follow my own path! Lol! It was GREAT no other ingredients needed!",
            "datePublished": "2019-10-20T00:21:18.393Z"
          },
          {
